# Airgap mirror sync — EXTERNAL (online) machine configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `mirrors.conf` (in the same directory) on the ONLINE
# machine that has access to GitHub. The real `mirrors.conf` is gitignored.
#
# This file MUST NOT contain any information about the internal/airgap
# network: no GitLab host, no group paths, no tokens. Those belong on the
# internal machine in `mirrors.internal.conf.example`.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local paths (deployment-specific)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bare clones live here. Each repo at: $MIRRORS_DIR/<name>.git
MIRRORS_DIR="${HOME}/mirrors"

# Bundle outputs land here. Copy this directory's contents to USB after
# running bundle-create.sh / releases-export.sh.
TRANSFER_DIR="${HOME}/usb-out"

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mirror catalog — name | github_owner/repo [| asset_policy]
#
# `name`              — local mirror folder name ($MIRRORS_DIR/<name>.git)
#                       AND the key used by the chart catalog
#                       (helm/redis-docs/files/external-links.yaml)
# `github_owner/repo` — upstream GitHub URL is https://github.com/<this>
# `asset_policy`      — OPTIONAL. Controls which Release ASSETS (binary
#                       uploads attached to GitHub Releases) get
#                       downloaded into $TRANSFER_DIR/releases/<name>/
#                       by releases-export.sh. Release metadata
#                       (title/body/tag) is always exported in full,
#                       regardless of policy.
#
#                       Values:
#                         (omitted) / all     download all assets   [default]
#                         none                metadata only — no binaries
#                         latest:N            assets for N most recent
#                                             releases (sliding window)
#                         since:YYYY-MM-DD    assets for releases
#                                             published on/after this date
#
# No GitLab path here — that's internal-only data.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Defaults below match a measured snapshot of the upstream repos:
#   RedisInsight ships ~5.8 GiB of GUI installers across 48 releases. The
#     latest release alone is ~1.07 GiB (10 platform-specific installers:
#     Windows .exe, macOS .dmg x64/arm64, Linux .deb/.rpm/.AppImage/.snap
#     across x86_64 and arm64). Set to `latest:1` so each export grabs
#     only the newest installer set; subsequent runs are no-ops until a
#     fresh upstream release lands, at which point only that single new
#     release's assets download.
#   prometheus-operator ships ~287 MiB across many small platform
#     binaries — kept as `all` since the operator is genuinely needed.
#   The remaining repos are tens of MiB or less; `all` (default) is fine.
#
# Total transfer on a clean external machine: ~1.4 GiB on first run,
# then small deltas (typically < 50 MiB per run unless RedisInsight ships
# a new release, in which case ~1 GiB for that one release).
MIRRORS=(
  "k8s-docs|RedisLabs/redis-enterprise-k8s-docs"
  "observability|redis-field-engineering/redis-enterprise-observability"
  "redis|redis/redis"
  "RediSearch|RediSearch/RediSearch"
  "RedisGraph|RedisGraph/RedisGraph"
  "RedisInsight|RedisInsight/RedisInsight|latest:1"
  "RedisTimeSeries|RedisTimeSeries/RedisTimeSeries"
  "RedisGears|RedisGears/RedisGears"
  "RedisJSON|RedisJSON/RedisJSON"
  "RedisBloom|RedisBloom/RedisBloom"
  "redis-py|redis/redis-py"
  "prometheus-operator|prometheus-operator/prometheus-operator"
)
